{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SigmaJGeometricCarrier","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PerLoopMeasureShadowAssembly"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.sharpened_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.sharpened_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L130-L139","doc":"**Sharpened assembly — the full B5 target from the SINGLE open field.**\nThe merged `shadow_assembly` took an open `f/hnorm/hint` triple (the Hodge\nassignment and its normalization + ρ-intertwining) as explicit hypotheses. Here\nthose are DISCHARGED — `f := hodgeShadow` with `shadow_norm` and\n`shadow_intertwines.1` (both automatic, from the FORCED assignment) — so the B4\ntarget `[2]_q · w(i) = w(i) + w(−i)` (the q→1 one-loop restoring the doubled\nunit) follows from ONLY `[PeriodMapWeight w]`, i.e. the single MOC field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.nome_equivariance_automatic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.nome_equivariance_automatic","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L120-L128","doc":"**Automatic — NOT a field: the nome anti-holomorphic equivariance shadow.**\nThe reality doubling is carried by `bar = conj`, which EXCHANGES the degenerate\npair (`conj i = −i`), while the transpose role-swap FIXES each point\n(`−conj i = i`) — reusing `bar_exchanges_degenerate_pair` /\n`transpose_fixes_degenerate_pair`. Audit §2: `τ(q̄) = −conj(τ(q))` is forced by\nthe nome `q = e^{2πiτ}`, so this is derived, not open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.involution_match_automatic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.involution_match_automatic","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L110-L118","doc":"**Automatic — NOT a field: the involution match `ρ ↔ Hodge conjugation`.**\nThe FORCED shadow assignment satisfies the ρ-intertwining unconditionally\n(`hodgeShadow (conj i) = ¬ hodgeShadow i`), reusing `shadow_intertwines`. Audit\n(2) `2026-08-02-hodge-lift-bring-h1-model.md`: `c = SWAP∘conj` is the canonical\nWeil real structure for ANY moduli, so this match carries no arithmetic content\nand is not an open field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.doubled_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.doubled_total","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L102-L106","doc":"**Derived (doubled total).** The selected channel `H^{1,0}` carries exactly\nhalf the pair total: `w(i) + w(−i) = 2·w(i)` — reusing the merged sorry-free\n`channel_share_is_half`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.equal_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.equal_split","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**Derived — this was the merged interface's second field (`conjugated`).**\nGiven the single MOC field, the loop weight splits equally across the conjugate\npair `{i, −i}`: `w(−i) = w(i)`. The ½ of the per-loop measure is now ρ-FORCED\nfrom the reality field alone — reusing the merged sorry-free\n`rho_forced_equal_split`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.selfAdjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.selfAdjoint","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The period-map image weight is real self-adjoint (ρ-symmetric): the shadow\nof the conformal Laplacian's reality. This is the single open MOC field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PeriodMapWeightReduction.PeriodMapWeight","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PeriodMapWeightReduction.lean#L65-L88","doc":"**Primary conjecture — the B2 lift, minimal open core (MOC), shadow form.**\n\nParameter: `w : GInt → Int`, the period-map image weight on the degenerate\nconjugate pair `{i, −i}` (the shadow of the conformal Laplacian carried by `Φ`\nonto the rank-2 sub-object `H¹(E_{τ(q)})`).\n\nThe single field `selfAdjoint` asserts the MOC's one substantive content: the\nweight is **real self-adjoint = ρ-symmetric** (`w (conj z) = w z`), i.e. the\nLaplacian data is real. This is the shadow of the matrix interface's `hermitian`\nfield; the second matrix field `conjugated` (the `H^{0,1}` weight is the\nconjugate of the `H^{1,0}` weight) is now DERIVED — see `equal_split` — and the\ninvolution-match + nome-equivariance are AUTOMATIC (`involution_match_automatic`,\n`nome_equivariance_automatic`), so neither is a field.\n\nOPEN: **no instance is declared.** The conjecture is exhibiting the specific `w`\nthat the categorical τ-functor's period map `Φ` produces for the actual α_EM\nloop weight — the framework's foundational q↔period bridge. Leaving this class\nuninstantiated is the honest open state (the MOC). Per §\"Axiomatization is NOT a\nProof\" the class axiomatises the lift's *input* (reality of the weight); every\ntheorem below derives its conclusion from that input, none closes the wall. ","signatureChunk":0}]}